# SAME70Q20B USB-CDC boot/connect smoke test. Exercises the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_USB firmware variant (the duet3-6hc / duet3-6xd printer
# configs are USB+CAN-only on real hardware; no serial-mode variant
# exists) against the local USBHS Renode peripheral
# (repl/same70_usbhs.cs), which injects a synthetic SET_CONFIGURATION
# SETUP on EP0 so klipper's CDC stack reaches bulk-active without a full
# USB host emulation, then exposes BULK_IN/BULK_OUT as a UART pipe.
# same70_smoke.test covers the CONFIG_ATSAM_SERIAL path; both share the
# same .repl (USBHS is resident and idle when unused).
#
# Two SAME70-specific details this pins down:
#   - same70q20b.repl pins systickFrequency to 300MHz. Upstream
#     platforms/cpus/sam_e70.repl declares SysTick at 450MHz, but klipper
#     drives it with CLKSOURCE=processor (the 300MHz core clock) and
#     reads DWT->CYCCNT at 300MHz. At 450MHz SysTick fires ~1.5x early,
#     so timer_dispatch_many busy-waits a far deadline while other timers
#     fall >1ms behind DWT -> "Rescheduled timer in the past" shutdown.
#   - same70_usbhs.cs injects the SETUP as soon as the firmware arms
#     RXSTPES on the allocated EP0, so enumeration self-starts
#     independent of the SysTick rate.
#
# This test stays free-run; same70_usb_tick.test drives the same USB-CDC
# link under tick lockstep.
DICTIONARY same70q20b-usb.dict
CONFIG same70_usb_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR same70_usb_smoke.fixture.json

M114
M105
M105
M105

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
